A version of GPT–6.2 Sol made for the Chat tab is rolling out to Plus, Pro, Business, and Enterprise tiers, <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes#november-23-2026">OpenAI said today</a>. OpenAI says GPT–6.2 Sol has been tweaked for everyday conversation and can more easily handle complex requests involving detailed instructions or locating information online.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/gpt-6-2-openai.jpg" alt="" width="1344" height="756" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079194" /><br/>
Compared with GPT–6, GPT–6.2 Sol does a better job detecting fine details in photos, like symbols on a sign or text on a label. It has improved at choosing options online based on the user's priorities, and it is smarter about when to offer a follow-up after a conversation, such as an alert about a price drop.<br/>
<br/>
OpenAI says the model scores higher in teen safety evaluations, with gains in areas like emotional reliance, disordered eating, dangerous activities, and age-restricted goods and services. The model meets OpenAI's safety policies in challenging conversations 91 to 94 percent of the time, up from 77 to 80 percent for GPT–6.<br/>
<br/>
